    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. One thing the stakeholder is worried about is the \"unpredictability\" factor—specifically, the fear that even with horizontal scaling, some random, unforeseen error could still cause a localized outage in one of the service instances and cascade through the system. How would you describe that kind of risk to them without getting too bogged down in the weeds of distributed systems theory?",
