      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While horizontal scaling handles predictable load well, we recognize that individual server failures can still ripple through the system if not managed correctly. To mitigate this, our strategy includes building in \"fail-safe\" mechanisms that automatically route traffic away from unhealthy nodes, much like a smart traffic director ensuring cars don't pile up on a jammed road. These safeguards, combined with automated testing and redundancy, are already in place to single out and isolate any unexpected errors before they impact the broader service. This ensures our approach remains robust even when unforeseen issues arise.",
      "source": "target",
